{'symbol': 'BK', 'date': '2023-01-13 06:42:00', 'title': 'BNY MELLON DECLARES DIVIDENDS', 'text': 'NEW YORK , JAN. 13, 2023 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- THE BANK OF NEW YORK MELLON CORPORATION (NYSE: BK) TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT ITS BOARD OF DIRECTORS DECLARED DIVIDENDS ON ITS COMMON AND PREFERRED STOCK AS FOLLOWS: COMMON – A QUARTERLY COMMON STOCK DIVIDEND OF $0.37 PER SHARE, PAYABLE ON FEBRUARY 3, 2023 TO SHAREHOLDERS OF RECORD AS OF THE CLOSE OF BUSINESS ON JANUARY 23, 2023. PREFERRED – THE FOLLOWING DIVIDENDS FOR THE NONCUMULATIVE PERPETUAL PREFERRED STOCK, LIQUIDATION PREFERENCE $100,000 PER SHARE, FOR THE DIVIDEND PERIOD ENDING IN MARCH 2023, IN EACH CASE PAYABLE ON MARCH\xa020, 2023 TO HOLDERS OF RECORD AS OF THE CLOSE OF BUSINESS ON MARCH\xa05, 2023: $1,327.72 PER SHARE ON THE SERIES A PREFERRED STOCK (EQUIVALENT TO $13.277150 PER NORMAL PREFERRED CAPITAL SECURITY OF MELLON CAPITAL IV, EACH REPRESENTING A 1/100TH INTEREST IN A SHARE OF THE SERIES A PREFERRED STOCK);\xa0 \xa0\xa0 $2,312.50 PER SHARE ON THE SERIES F PREFERRED STOCK (EQUIVALENT TO $23.125000 PER DEPOSITARY SHARE, EACH REPRESENTING A 1/100TH INTEREST IN A SHARE OF THE SERIES F PREFERRED STOCK);\xa0 $2,350.00 PER SHARE ON THE SERIES G PREFERRED STOCK (EQUIVALENT TO $23.500000 PER DEPOSITARY SHARE, EACH REPRESENTING A 1/100TH INTEREST IN A SHARE OF THE SERIES G PREFERRED STOCK); $925.00 PER SHARE ON THE SERIES H PREFERRED STOCK (EQUIVALENT TO $9.250000 PER DEPOSITARY SHARE, EACH REPRESENTING A 1/100TH INTEREST IN A SHARE OF THE SERIES H PREFERRED STOCK); AND $937.50 PER SHARE ON THE SERIES I PREFERRED STOCK (EQUIVALENT TO $9.375000 PER DEPOSITARY SHARE, EACH REPRESENTING A 1/100TH INTEREST IN A SHARE OF THE SERIES I PREFERRED STOCK).'}{'symbol': 'BK', 'date': '2023-01-13 06:41:00', 'title': 'BNY MELLON REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER 2022 RESULTS', 'text': "NEW YORK , JAN. 13, 2023 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- BNY MELLON\xa0HAS REPORTED FINANCIAL RESULTS FOR THE FOURTH QUARTER 2022. THE COMPANY'S EARNINGS RELEASE ALONG WITH THE QUARTERLY FINANCIAL HIGHLIGHTS AND OTHER EARNINGS-RELATED DOCUMENTS ARE AVAILABLE AT WWW.BNYMELLON.COM/INVESTORRELATIONS."}